==Old English==

===Etymology===
{{root|ang|ine-pro|*dyew-}}
from {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*Tīwas dagaz||Tuesday|lit=Tiw's Day}}, from {{m|gem-pro|*Tīwaz||Tyr, god of war}} + {{m|gem-pro|*dagaz||day}}. This was a [[interpretatio germanica|Germanic interpretation]] of {{cog|la|dies Martis}}, itself a translation of {{cog|grc|Ἄρεως ἡμέρα}} ({{w|interpretatio romana}}).

